=== PARITY (vs web AiLimitBanner.tsx) ===
  Data source -> the web component is a fully controlled presentational leaf; its only hook is
    useTranslation. That maps to the P1/S10 ALBStrings facade. The structured limit + the lifecycle
    around it (the parent's useAiStream `limit` field) bind through the shared P1/S8 state-holder
    seam (AiLimitBannerSource -> AiLimitBannerModel); the view performs NO HTTP.
  Reason taxonomy -> AiLimitReason ports BOTH web switch tables (titleForReason / descriptionForReason)
    EXACTLY: 11 named wire reasons, input_tokens+output_tokens collapsed onto one "token quota" title/
    desc, missing_feature_id+unknown_feature_id collapsed onto one "misconfigured" title/desc, and any
    unrecognized reason → the generic copy (the web `default:` branch; .other preserves the raw wire
    value for the data-reason hook). Unit-asserted key-for-key.
  Level -> AiLimitBannerLevel reproduces the web variant ternary: critical → danger, warn → warning,
    else (incl. "") → info. Tone + SF Symbol are unit-tested.
  Countdown -> AiLimitCountdown.tick is a 1:1 port of `setSecondsLeft((s) => (s > 0 ? s - 1 : 0))`;
    retry-ready is `secondsLeft <= 0`. The Model seeds secondsLeft from retryAfterS (floored at 0),
    runs a once-per-second Task, and re-seeds on each distinct limit (the web useEffect keyed on info).
    The arithmetic + the gate are unit-tested deterministically (the native parallel of the web
    fake-timer tests; automaticCountdown:false drives tick() by hand).
  Composition -> AiLimitBannerCard mirrors the shared TSAlertBanner (tone fill 0.1 + stroke 0.3,
    TSRadius.md): leading severity SF Symbol, reason-keyed title + description, the "try again in N"
    line shown ONLY while !retryReady (web parity), a trailing dismiss control, and the two actions.
  Shared components -> @/components/feedback maps to TSAlertBanner (banner), TSSkeleton (loading),
    ContentUnavailableView (empty), and the TSErrorDisplay/TSBadge looks (error retry + stale/offline
    chips). @/components/ui/Button maps to TSButton — "Use baseline" (variant ghost, size small) and
    "Retry" (variant primary, size small), gated EXACTLY like the web: baseline shows when
    `onUseBaseline && info.baselineAvailable` (native canUseBaseline && row.baselineAvailable); retry
    shows when `onRetry && retryReady` (native canRetry && retryReady). Recharts/Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> the web leaf returns null when info==null; the native surface owns the full
    P4 states contract around the parent stream:
      loading -> a redacted TSSkeleton banner row (initial limit check);
      empty   -> a friendly ContentUnavailableView ("Helix is available") — the never-a-blank-box
                 native treatment of the web `if (!info) return null` (the healthy no-limit outcome,
                 and the surface a user dismiss falls back to);
      banner  -> the faithful active-limit card across all severities + the live countdown;
      error   -> the stream-failure branch (TSQueryError equivalent + a native retry -> source.refresh);
      stale   -> a "This notice may be out of date" chip + a single auto-refresh on each rising edge
                 into the stale window (unit-tested);
      offline -> an "Offline — showing the last Helix status" chip over the cached banner.
    Each state has a #if DEBUG preview (9 total) + a unit test.
  i18n -> all 23 web-source keys (10 titles + 10 descriptions + useBaseline + retry + retryIn) resolve
    through the P1/S10 facade with the web English fallback (coverage asserted). Plus 7 native chrome/
    a11y keys (loading, empty title/message, error message, stale, offline, dismiss). No English literal
    in Swift (Text(verbatim:) over the facade; inline English lives only in the ALBText fallbacks).
  a11y -> the banner copy block is one .ignore element with a composed VoiceOver label (title +
    description + the countdown line while counting); the leading icon is hidden; the dismiss + baseline
    + retry buttons and each status chip carry an accessibilityLabel; the card carries the
    accessibilityIdentifier "ai-limit-banner" (the data-reason parity hook); Dynamic Type via tokens;
    Reduce Motion gates the TSSkeleton shimmer.
  Telemetry -> AiLimitBannerModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"AiLimitBanner") -> bridges the
    shared Telemetry.track (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once, idempotent start).

